module engine where

-- =========================================================================
-- analyze.fenel — the ANALYZE skeleton + the call-graph SCC discovery + the
-- advisory totality census over a function registry.
-- unified-static-analysis Phase 3f. Brief:
-- `workstreams/unified-static-analysis/briefs/phase-3f-totality-gate-analyze-skeleton-scc-census.md`.
--
-- THE MEASUREMENT + INTEGRATION SLICE the kernel gate (3g) is conditioned on.
-- Phases 1 / 3a / 3c / 3d / 3e shipped the whole termination band — rung-1
-- (structural) → rung-2 (guarded measure) → rung-3a (lexicographic) → rung-3b
-- (size-change graph closure, ONE function) → rung-3c (`checkMutualTotality`
-- over a SET of functions). But `checkMutualTotality` takes the
-- mutually-recursive set as an EXPLICIT input (3e D-3e-4: slice C does NOT
-- discover WHICH functions form a cycle), and the checker has NEVER run over
-- real code (the 51 totality tests are all hand-built `Expr` fixtures). THIS
-- module closes both gaps:
--   (a) the call-graph SCC DISCOVERY that feeds `checkMutualTotality` its groups
--       (each strongly-connected component = one mutually-recursive group;
--       a non-recursive function = a singleton SCC), and
--   (b) the `analyze` SKELETON (registry functions → per-SCC totality verdict →
--       a `Total / Unknown / Partial / Unanalyzable` census).
-- It is kernel-SAFE: NO kernel mutation, NO `PropForall` wiring, NO
-- `Unknown`→reject flip (that is the SUCCESSOR slice 3g, which the census
-- informs). ADVISORY ONLY (D-3f-5).
--
-- WHY FENEL (the Fenel-first HARD rule). The call-graph builder + SCC pass +
-- analyze skeleton are PURE graph/walk logic — no IO, no host primitive — so
-- they are Fenel bodies. The SCC closure uses a finite node-count-derived exact
-- fixpoint bound and a self-tail loop; the call-graph walk REUSES the
-- `Expr` tree-walk SHAPE from `totality.fenel`. The ONLY new TS is the census
-- RUNNER (`scripts/totality-census.ts`, test/tooling category) that gathers
-- host-side registry data, lowers stored JSON-Logic bodies to core `Expr`
-- (via the shipped `jsonLogicToExpr`), and prints the census — NO graph/analysis
-- decision lives in TS.
--
-- SCC = MUTUAL-REACHABILITY CLOSURE, not Tarjan (D-3f-1). Two nodes `u, v` are
-- in the same SCC iff `u →* v AND v →* u`. For an ADVISORY census correctness ≫
-- performance, and the reachability formulation is the transitive closure of the
-- call-graph edge relation — repeated squaring
-- `R_{k+1} = R_k ∪ (R_k ; R_k)` until fixpoint. The finite node set supplies
-- the exact `|V| + 1` round bound; the self-tail loop compiles stack-safe. Tarjan's
-- explicit-stack lowlink DFS is faster but painful + error-prone in a pure
-- functional body (mutable stack + index state) and buys nothing for an advisory
-- pass. No repository-size constant or partial-closure fallback remains.
--
-- ONLY group-INTERNAL edges matter. The call graph's nodes are the registry's
-- functions; an edge `f → g` exists iff `f`'s body calls `g` OR references it
-- by name (`EVar` — effect-visibility Phase 1) AND `g` is a registry function.
-- Stored bodies keep SOURCE spellings (bare code names, `Module.name`, var-head
-- `$dyn:` calls) while ids are canonical `module:name`, so callees are matched
-- through `anaSpellingTargets` (2026-10-02: the exact-membership test it
-- replaced matched almost no real call, and every Fenel-bodied system function
-- read Total at the kernel gate). A bare name over-approximates to every id
-- with that code name; `totHeadMayName` applies the same normalization when the
-- size-change walk matches call heads to group members. A call to a
-- `std:`/native/`@native` LEAF (an id with no body) is a sink only when the leaf
-- is certified (anaCertifiedNativeLeaves, decided by verdictTagForIn before the
-- analysis; 2026-10-03 — before, every bodyless id was assumed total). A
-- bound variable that shadows a function name is a conservative
-- over-approximation (an extra harmless edge, never a missing obligation).
--
-- CENSUS vs GATE. The census (`analyzeFunctions` / `censusFunctions`) reports
-- each SCC's OWN verdict: a group calling a non-total group outside itself, or
-- an Unanalyzable body (excluded from the call graph, D-3f-4), still counts its
-- own verdict, so the census is a per-group worklist, not a transitive
-- certificate. The kernel-gate projection `verdictTagFor` IS transitive: every
-- group the subject reaches must be Total, and a reached Unanalyzable body makes
-- it Unknown. A partition that MERGES non-mutual functions only adds graphs (a
-- false-`Unknown` at worst, never a false-`Total`).
--
-- INPUT. A function is the plain record `{ id, params, body, declaredPartial,
-- analyzable }` (0 entity decls — the propagate.fenel/totality.fenel
-- plain-record discipline):
--   • id             : String       — the registry fn-id (the call-graph node key)
--   • params         : List String  — parameter names (the `checkMutualTotality` shape)
--   • body           : Expr         — the LOWERED core Expr (meaningless when not analyzable)
--   • declaredPartial: Bool         — the `@partial` escape-hatch flag
--   • analyzable     : Bool         — False when the stored JSON-Logic body did NOT
--                                     lower to core `Expr` (the 56 `Err` cases); such
--                                     a function is bucketed `Unanalyzable` and EXCLUDED
--                                     from the census call graph (D-3f-4); the gate
--                                     projection refuses any subject that reaches it.
--                                     NEVER folded into Total.
-- The lowering to core `Expr` happens in the census RUNNER (the `$`-key marshal
-- barrier: a `.fenel` body cannot walk raw JSON-Logic, whose keys ARE evaluator
-- ops); the Fenel bodies here see only core `Expr`.
-- =========================================================================


-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- A. The call-graph builder. `analyzeCallees` walks a core `Expr` body and
-- collects every id of `knownIds` (the registry's function-id set) that an
-- `ECall` head or an `EVar` reference may denote (spelling-normalized,
-- `anaSpellingTargets`), deduped. The `EVar`
-- arm (effect-visibility Phase 1) closes the var-blindness hole: a function
-- referenced by BARE NAME — argument position (`map helper xs`) or let-value
-- position (`let x = listSystemEntities`) — is a reach edge exactly like a
-- call head; a non-member `EVar` stays a plain data var (no edge, and NO
-- `$dyn` — the referent of a resolvable name is statically known, so its
-- requires flow precisely). REUSES the `totality.fenel` walk shape (recurse the
-- 7-case `Expr`); a spelling bound by an enclosing lambda or arm pattern is a
-- local and adds no edge (exact), while a function parameter that shadows a
-- function name is not visible to the walk and may yield a FALSE edge, which
-- only ADDS requires / blocks purity — sound direction). A spelling that denotes no known id (a data var,
-- a field read, a builtin op) adds nothing.
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@label "analyze: add unique name"
@description "Append `name` to `acc` only if not already present (dedup). Used to collect a deduped callee list."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaAddUnique : (name: String) -> (acc: a) -> a
anaAddUnique name acc = if elem name acc then acc else appendItem name acc

@label "analyze: collect callees in arg list"
@description "Fold anaCalleesIn over a list of argument/child expressions, threading the deduped callee accumulator."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaCalleesInList : (knownIds: a) -> (acc: b) -> (args: c) -> b
anaCalleesInList knownIds acc args =
  fold (\current a -> anaCalleesIn knownIds current a) acc args

@label "analyze: collect callees in match arms"
@description "Fold anaCalleesIn over each match arm's guard (when present — it runs before the body) and body (arm pattern bindings do not affect callee collection — the conservative over-approx). Threads the accumulator."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaCalleesInArms : (knownIds: a) -> (acc: b) -> (arms: c) -> b
anaCalleesInArms knownIds acc arms =
  fold
    (\current arm ->
      case lookup arm "guard" of
        Nothing -> anaCalleesIn knownIds current arm.body
        Just guard -> anaCalleesIn knownIds (anaCalleesIn knownIds current guard) arm.body)
    acc
    arms

@label "analyze: collect callees in record fields"
@description "Fold anaCalleesIn over a record's field values ({name, value} records). Threads the accumulator."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaCalleesInFields : (knownIds: a) -> (acc: b) -> (fields: c) -> b
anaCalleesInFields knownIds acc fields =
  fold (\current f -> anaCalleesIn knownIds current f.value) acc fields

@label "analyze: spelling targets"
@description "The knownIds a call-head or variable spelling may denote. Stored bodies keep their source spellings (bare code names, `Module.name`, var-head `$dyn:` calls) while registry ids are canonical `module:name`, so an exact-membership test missed nearly every real call (2026-10-02: every Fenel-bodied system function, std:map included, was vacuously Total at the kernel gate). Normalization: strip `$dyn:`; the exact id; a dotted spelling is the id whose last dot reads as the colon (`publicdemo.statistics.f` ⇒ `publicdemo.statistics:f`); a bare name is EVERY id whose code name it is (an import or the module's own definition: over-approximated across modules, which only adds call-graph edges); any other colon spelling names nothing known. `joined` is anaJoinedIds knownIds, so a bare name costs one native substring test (and one split when it matches). A spelling that is a local variable may gain a spurious edge — harmless (the conservative direction). Field reads (`row.args`) find no id."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
anaSpellingTargets : (spelling: String) -> (knownIds: a) -> (joined: String) -> a
anaSpellingTargets spelling knownIds joined =
  let name = if startsWith spelling "$dyn:" then slice spelling 5 (length spelling) else spelling
  if elem name knownIds then appendItem name []
  else if contains name ":" then []
  else if contains name "." then
    let parts = split name "."
    let canonical = concat (join (fromMaybe [] (init parts)) ".") (concat ":" (fromMaybe name (last parts)))
    if elem canonical knownIds then appendItem canonical [] else []
  else
    let marker = concat ":" (concat name ",")
    if not (contains joined marker) then []
    else
      let pieces = fromMaybe [] (init (split joined marker))
      map (\piece -> concat (fromMaybe "" (last (split piece ","))) (concat ":" name)) pieces

@label "analyze: add spelling targets"
@description "Add every knownId a spelling may denote (anaSpellingTargets) to the deduped callee accumulator. `joined` is the comma-framed id list anaJoinedIds builds once per body."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
anaAddSpellingTargets : (spelling: String) -> (knownIds: a) -> (joined: String) -> (acc: b) -> b
anaAddSpellingTargets spelling knownIds joined acc =
  fold (\current target -> anaAddUnique target current) acc (anaSpellingTargets spelling knownIds joined)

@label "analyze: joined ids"
@description "The known ids framed as one comma-separated string with a leading and trailing comma (`,a:f,b:g,`). A bare spelling `n` denotes exactly the ids whose text is preceded by a comma and ends with `:n,`, so one native substring test settles the common no-match case (locals, builtins) and one native split recovers each matching module; registry ids hold no comma."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
anaJoinedIds : (knownIds: a) -> String
anaJoinedIds knownIds = concat "," (concat (join knownIds ",") ",")

@label "analyze: spellings in a body"
@description "Walk the 7-case core Expr collecting every ECall head and every EVar name, deduped, in first-occurrence order: the raw spellings anaCalleesIn resolves once each. A list literal's synthetic `appendItem` (totIsListLiteral) is a construction, not a call: its elements are walked, its head is not collected. The apply form `$` is application, a language-core form the evaluator runs directly (never a call to the registry's `($)` function): its head is not collected, its callee and arguments are walked (the group audit judges what it invokes, totUncheckedApply). A variable, or a var-head (`$dyn:`) call, whose root (totSpellingRoot) an enclosing lambda or arm pattern binds is a local and is skipped (exact: such a spelling denotes the local, never a function; the function's own params are not visible here and stay conservative). ELambda/EMatch (arm guards included — a guard runs before its body)/EConstruct/ERecord recurse their subterms."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
anaSpellingsIn : (bound: a) -> (acc: a) -> (e: (Expr Any)) -> a
anaSpellingsIn bound acc e =
  case e of
    ELit { value = _ } -> acc
    EVar { name = n } -> if elem (totSpellingRoot n) bound then acc else anaAddUnique n acc
    ECall { fnId = f, args = args } ->
      let withHead = if eq f "$" then acc else if totIsListLiteral e then acc else if startsWith f "$dyn:" then (if elem (totSpellingRoot f) bound then acc else anaAddUnique f acc) else anaAddUnique f acc
      fold (\current a -> anaSpellingsIn bound current a) withHead args
    ELambda { params = ps, body = bd } -> anaSpellingsIn (totAppendAll ps bound) acc bd
    EMatch { scrutinee = s, arms = arms } ->
      fold
        (\current arm ->
          case lookup arm "guard" of
            Nothing -> anaSpellingsIn (totCollectAllVars arm.pattern bound) current arm.body
            Just guard -> anaSpellingsIn (totCollectAllVars arm.pattern bound) (anaSpellingsIn (totCollectAllVars arm.pattern bound) current guard) arm.body)
        (anaSpellingsIn bound acc s)
        arms
    EConstruct { args = args } -> fold (\current a -> anaSpellingsIn bound current a) acc args
    ERecord { fields = fields } -> fold (\current f -> anaSpellingsIn bound current f.value) acc fields

@label "analyze: collect callees against a joined id list"
@description "anaCalleesIn with the comma-framed id string (anaJoinedIds knownIds) supplied by the caller, so a caller resolving many bodies against one id list builds it once (verdictTagForIn)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
anaCalleesJoined : (knownIds: a) -> (joined: String) -> (e: (Expr Any)) -> b
anaCalleesJoined knownIds joined e =
  fold (\current spelling -> anaAddSpellingTargets spelling knownIds joined current) [] (anaSpellingsIn [] [] e)

@label "analyze: collect callees (walk)"
@description "Collect every knownId an ECall head OR an EVar name of the core Expr may denote into the deduped accumulator: the body's distinct spellings (anaSpellingsIn, guards included) each resolved once through anaSpellingTargets, so canonical, dotted, bare and var-head spellings of one function all reach its id. EVar is the var-ref callee edge (effect-visibility Phase 1 — a fn referenced by name in argument/let-value position is a reach edge like a call head; a data var finds no id, no edge and no $dyn). A spelling bound by an enclosing lambda or arm pattern is skipped (it denotes the local); a function parameter that shadows a function name is not visible here and may add a false edge, which only adds requires or gathers one more function — sound. The TS perf-branch mirror is collectCalledFunctions(includeVarRefs) in constraint-inference.ts."
@tags "engine" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f" "effect-visibility" "phase-1"
anaCalleesIn : (knownIds: a) -> (acc: b) -> (e: (Expr Any)) -> b
anaCalleesIn knownIds acc e =
  let joined = anaJoinedIds knownIds
  fold (\current spelling -> anaAddSpellingTargets spelling knownIds joined current) acc (anaSpellingsIn [] [] e)

@label "analyze: callees of a body"
@description "The deduped list of registry-function callees of a core Expr body: the knownIds its call heads and EVar references may denote under spelling normalization (anaSpellingTargets; the effect-visibility Phase 1 var-ref edge included). Seeds anaCalleesIn with an empty accumulator. The directed call-graph edges out of a function; the kernel gate's reachable-set gather (kernel.ts subjectTotalityVerdict) follows exactly these."
@tags "engine" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
analyzeCallees : (body: (Expr Any)) -> (knownIds: a) -> b
analyzeCallees body knownIds = anaCalleesIn knownIds [] body


-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Function-list helpers — the id projection, the analyzable filter, the
-- direct-edge build. An edge is the plain record `{ from, to }` (caller →
-- callee, both registry function ids). 0 entity decls.
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@label "analyze: map ids (tail)"
@description "Recurse on the tail of the function list for anaMapIds (keeps it free of case-in-let)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaMapIdsTail : (functions: a) -> a
anaMapIdsTail functions =
  case tail functions of
    Nothing -> []
    Just rest -> anaMapIds rest

@label "analyze: map ids"
@description "Project the `id` field of every function in the list into a List String (the call-graph node set / a group's member-id list). Order-irrelevant (used as a set)."
@tags "engine" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
anaMapIds : (functions: a) -> b
anaMapIds functions = map (\f -> f.id) functions

@label "analyze: filter analyzable (tail)"
@description "Recurse on the tail of the function list for anaFilterAnalyzable (keeps it free of case-in-let)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaFilterAnalyzableTail : (functions: a) -> a
anaFilterAnalyzableTail functions =
  case tail functions of
    Nothing -> []
    Just rest -> anaFilterAnalyzable rest

@label "analyze: filter analyzable"
@description "Keep only the functions whose `analyzable` flag is True (a body that lowered to core Expr). The Unanalyzable functions (the 56 Err cases) are EXCLUDED from the call graph — their callers lose that edge (sound under-approx; D-3f-4) — and counted separately by anaCountUnanalyzable."
@tags "engine" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
anaFilterAnalyzable : (functions: a) -> a
anaFilterAnalyzable functions = filter (\f -> f.analyzable) functions

@label "analyze: edges from one function"
@description "Build the direct call-graph edges {from, to} out of one function: for each deduped callee `c`, an edge {from = fromId, to = c}. Edges built via a `let` then the literal (the inline-record-in-arg surprise)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaEdgesFrom : (fromId: String) -> (callees: a) -> (acc: b) -> b
anaEdgesFrom fromId callees acc =
  concat acc (map (\c -> { from = fromId, to = c }) callees)

@label "analyze: build direct edges"
@description "Build the full directed call-graph edge set {from, to} over a function list: for each function, its callees ∩ knownIds become edges. Concatenated across functions (order-irrelevant — used as a relation)."
@tags "engine" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
anaBuildEdges : (functions: a) -> (knownIds: b) -> c
anaBuildEdges functions knownIds =
  fold
    (\edges f -> anaEdgesFrom f.id (analyzeCallees f.body knownIds) edges)
    []
    functions


-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- B. The reachability closure. The transitive closure of the {from, to} edge relation under
-- composition: `R_{k+1} = R_k ∪ { {a, c} : {a, b} ∈ R_k ∧ {b, c} ∈ R_k }`,
-- early-exit on no-change, with an exact finite `|V| + 1` caller bound. The
-- fixpoint helper is self-tail so compiled execution uses a loop. An edge is a {from, to} record;
-- a relation is a deduped `List {from, to}`.
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@label "analyze: edge eq"
@description "Equality of two call-graph edges: same `from` AND same `to` node. Drives dedup + set-equality of the reachability relation."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaEdgeEq : (e1: a) -> (e2: a) -> Bool
anaEdgeEq e1 e2 = if eq e1.from e2.from then eq e1.to e2.to else False

@label "analyze: edge member"
@description "True when edge `e` (exact from/to) occurs in relation `r`. Fold anaEdgeEq over r."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaEdgeMember : (e: a) -> (r: b) -> Bool
anaEdgeMember e r = fold (\found e2 -> if found then True else anaEdgeEq e e2) False r

@label "analyze: add edge unique"
@description "Insert edge `e` into relation `r` only if not already present (dedup). Keeps the relation a set."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaAddEdgeUnique : (e: a) -> (r: b) -> b
anaAddEdgeUnique e r = if anaEdgeMember e r then r else appendItem e r

@label "analyze: compose add"
@description "Add the composed edge {from = e1.from, to = e2.to} (the path through the matching intermediate e1.to == e2.from) to the accumulator, deduped. Built via a `let` then the literal."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaComposeAdd : (e1: a) -> (e2: a) -> (acc: b) -> b
anaComposeAdd e1 e2 acc =
  let e = { from = e1.from, to = e2.to }
  anaAddEdgeUnique e acc

@label "analyze: compose pair"
@description "If e1 and e2 meet at an intermediate (e1.to == e2.from), add the composed edge e1.from → e2.to; else leave the accumulator unchanged. One transitive-closure composition step."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaComposePair : (e1: a) -> (e2: a) -> (acc: b) -> b
anaComposePair e1 e2 acc =
  if eq e1.to e2.from then anaComposeAdd e1 e2 acc else acc

@label "analyze: compose inner (e1 over r)"
@description "Fold one edge e1 against every edge of r, adding each meeting composition to the accumulator. Inner loop of one closure round."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaComposeInner : (e1: a) -> (r: b) -> (acc: c) -> c
anaComposeInner e1 r acc =
  fold (\current e2 -> anaComposePair e1 e2 current) acc r

@label "analyze: compose outer (r over r)"
@description "Fold every edge of `gs` as e1 against the full relation `allR` (via anaComposeInner), accumulating the composed edges. Outer loop of one closure round."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaComposeOuter : (allR: a) -> (gs: b) -> (acc: c) -> c
anaComposeOuter allR gs acc =
  fold (\current e1 -> anaComposeInner e1 allR current) acc gs

@label "analyze: reach round"
@description "One closure round: `r` plus the composition of every meeting edge pair, deduped. Seeds the accumulator with `r` itself, so the round is non-shrinking (next ⊇ r)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaReachRound : (r: a) -> a
anaReachRound r = anaComposeOuter r r r

@label "analyze: edges subset"
@description "True when every edge of relation `s1` occurs in `s2`. Half of the closure fixpoint stop-test."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaEdgesSubset : (s1: a) -> (s2: b) -> Bool
anaEdgesSubset s1 s2 = fold (\contained e -> if contained then anaEdgeMember e s2 else False) True s1

@label "analyze: edge set eq"
@description "Set-equality of two relations (mutual edge-subset) — the closure fixpoint stop-test (the round added no new edge)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaEdgeSetEq : (s1: a) -> (s2: b) -> Bool
anaEdgeSetEq s1 s2 = totAnd (anaEdgesSubset s1 s2) (anaEdgesSubset s2 s1)

@label "analyze: reach close step"
@description "Stack-safe self-tail fixpoint loop. Compute the next squaring round; return at equality, otherwise continue with the expanded relation until the exact node-derived round bound is exhausted. The self-tail call compiles to the standard loop form."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaReachCloseStep : (fuel: a) -> (r: b) -> b
anaReachCloseStep fuel r =
  let next = anaReachRound r
  if anaEdgeSetEq next r then r else if eq fuel 0 then next else anaReachCloseStep (sub fuel 1) next

@label "analyze: reach close (bounded exact fixpoint)"
@description "The transitive closure of the call-graph edge relation under repeated squaring. Callers derive `fuel` from the finite node set (`|V| + 1`), which is an exact deterministic bound rather than a repository-size constant. The loop saturates in ceil(log2(longest-path)) rounds and anaReachCloseStep is self-tail/compiled stack-safe."
@tags "engine" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
anaReachClose : (fuel: a) -> (r: b) -> b
anaReachClose fuel r =
  if eq fuel 0 then r else anaReachCloseStep (sub fuel 1) r


-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The SCC partition (mutual-reachability grouping). `u, v` are in the same SCC
-- iff `u == v` OR (`u →* v` AND `v →* u`) over the reachability closure. A
-- non-recursive function is a singleton group. Each group is exactly the
-- `checkMutualTotality` input shape (the member records carry id/params/body —
-- extra fields are ignored by the checker).
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@label "analyze: reachable"
@description "True when node `a` reaches node `b` in the closed relation `r` (the edge {from = a, to = b} is present). Built via a `let` then anaEdgeMember."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaReachable : (a: String) -> (b: String) -> (r: c) -> Bool
anaReachable a b r =
  let e = { from = a, to = b }
  anaEdgeMember e r

@label "analyze: same SCC"
@description "True when `u` and `v` are in the same strongly-connected component: the same node (u == v), or MUTUALLY reachable (u →* v AND v →* u) in the closed relation. The SCC equivalence the partition groups by."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaSameScc : (u: String) -> (v: String) -> (r: a) -> Bool
anaSameScc u v r =
  if eq u v then True else totAnd (anaReachable u v r) (anaReachable v u r)

@label "analyze: members of (tail)"
@description "Recurse on the tail of the function list for anaMembersOf (keeps it free of case-in-let)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaMembersOfTail : (fid: String) -> (functions: a) -> (r: b) -> a
anaMembersOfTail fid functions r =
  case tail functions of
    Nothing -> []
    Just rest -> anaMembersOf fid rest r

@label "analyze: members of"
@description "Every function in the list that is in the same SCC as node `fid` (the SCC group of fid). Keeps the full function records (id/params/body/… — the checkMutualTotality input)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaMembersOf : (fid: String) -> (functions: a) -> (r: b) -> a
anaMembersOf fid functions r = filter (\g -> anaSameScc fid g.id r) functions

@label "analyze: group-by skip"
@description "Advance to the tail of the `remaining` worklist, threading the `assigned` id-set unchanged. Used both for an already-assigned head and after emitting a group."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaGroupBySkip : (allFns: a) -> (remaining: b) -> (r: c) -> (assigned: d) -> e
anaGroupBySkip allFns remaining r assigned =
  case tail remaining of
    Nothing -> []
    Just rest -> anaGroupByGo allFns rest r assigned

@label "analyze: group-by emit"
@description "Emit the SCC group of the worklist head `f`: collect all members in f's SCC (anaMembersOf over the FULL function list), mark their ids assigned, and prepend the group to the partition built from the rest of the worklist (threading the grown assigned set)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaGroupByEmit : (allFns: a) -> (remaining: b) -> (r: c) -> (assigned: d) -> (f: e) -> g
anaGroupByEmit allFns remaining r assigned f =
  let members = anaMembersOf f.id allFns r
  let memberIds = anaMapIds members
  let assigned2 = totConcat memberIds assigned
  let restGroups = anaGroupBySkip allFns remaining r assigned2
  appendItem members restGroups

@label "analyze: group-by walk"
@description "Walk the worklist, emitting one group per not-yet-assigned head (its whole SCC) and skipping already-assigned heads. Threads the `assigned` id-set so each SCC is emitted once. Helper for sccPartition."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaGroupByGo : (allFns: a) -> (remaining: b) -> (r: c) -> (assigned: d) -> e
anaGroupByGo allFns remaining r assigned =
  let partitioned =
        fold
          (\state f ->
            if elem f.id state.assigned then state
            else
              let members = anaMembersOf f.id allFns r
              { groups = appendItem members state.groups, assigned = totConcat (anaMapIds members) state.assigned })
          { groups = [], assigned = assigned }
          remaining
  partitioned.groups

@label "analyze: SCC partition"
@description "Partition a function list into its strongly-connected components (each SCC = one mutually-recursive group; a non-recursive function = a singleton group). Builds the direct call-graph edges (callees ∩ the function ids), takes the exact finite reachability closure using a node-count-derived bound, then groups by mutual reachability. Each group is exactly the checkMutualTotality input shape (its members carry id/params/body). The bridge from `a checker over a given group` (3e) to `a checker over the program` — the gap 3e left (D-3e-4)."
@tags "engine" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
sccPartition : (functions: a) -> b
sccPartition functions =
  let knownIds = anaMapIds functions
  let edges = anaBuildEdges functions knownIds
  let closure = anaReachClose (add (length functions) 1) edges
  anaGroupByGo functions functions closure []


-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- C. The analyze skeleton. `analyzeGroup` runs `checkMutualTotality` over a
-- group's members; the `@partial` fold makes a group `Partial` when ANY member
-- is declared `@partial` (D-3f-3 — the escape-hatch is per-definition; the
-- simplest sound aggregation). `analyzeFunctions` = sccPartition then
-- analyzeGroup per group. `censusFunctions` aggregates into the count census +
-- the `Unknown` id worklist.
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@label "analyze: group has @partial member"
@description "True when ANY member of the group is declared @partial (declaredPartial). The per-group @partial fold (D-3f-3)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaGroupHasPartial : (group: a) -> Bool
anaGroupHasPartial group =
  fold (\found m -> if found then True else m.declaredPartial) False group

@label "analyze: analyze one group"
@description "The verdict for ONE SCC group: Partial when any member is declared @partial (D-3f-3), else the rung-3c checkMutualTotality verdict (Total | Unknown) over the group's {id, params, body} members. Returns {ids, verdict} — the member ids the verdict covers, plus the three-valued Totality. The headline compose: SCC-discovery + checkMutualTotality certify (or flag) a real mutual group."
@tags "engine" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
analyzeGroup : (group: a) -> b
analyzeGroup group =
  let ids = anaMapIds group
  let verdict = if anaGroupHasPartial group then Partial { reason = "group has a declared @partial member" } else checkMutualTotality group
  { ids = ids, verdict = verdict }

@label "analyze: analyze each group (tail)"
@description "Recurse on the tail of the group list for anaAnalyzeGroups (keeps it free of case-in-let)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaAnalyzeGroupsTail : (groups: a) -> b
anaAnalyzeGroupsTail groups =
  case tail groups of
    Nothing -> []
    Just rest -> anaAnalyzeGroups rest

@label "analyze: analyze each group"
@description "Map analyzeGroup over every SCC group, yielding a List {ids, verdict}."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaAnalyzeGroups : (groups: a) -> b
anaAnalyzeGroups groups = map (\g -> analyzeGroup g) groups

@label "analyze: analyze functions"
@description "The analyze skeleton: filter the analyzable functions (the Unanalyzable bodies are excluded from the call graph — their callers lose that edge, sound under-approx), partition into SCCs (sccPartition), and run analyzeGroup per group. Returns a List {ids, verdict} — one entry per SCC. The per-function lowering of a stored JSON-Logic body to core Expr (via jsonLogicToExpr) happens in the census RUNNER BEFORE this (so both callee-extraction and the totality walk see core Expr)."
@tags "engine" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
analyzeFunctions : (functions: a) -> b
analyzeFunctions functions =
  let analyzable = anaFilterAnalyzable functions
  let groups = sccPartition analyzable
  anaAnalyzeGroups groups


-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The census. Aggregate analyzeFunctions into the count census + the Unknown id
-- worklist; the Unanalyzable functions are counted separately (NEVER folded into
-- Total — D-3f-4). The counts are by MEMBER-ID COUNT (a 2-member Unknown group
-- contributes 2 to `unknown`, not 1), so the census counts functions, not SCCs.
-- The census record `{total, unknown, partial, unanalyzable, unknownIds}` is the
-- phase's headline output.
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@label "analyze: census bump total"
@description "Add `n` to the census accumulator's `total` count, leaving the others. Returns the updated census record."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaBumpTotal : (acc: a) -> (n: b) -> a
anaBumpTotal acc n =
  { total = add acc.total n, unknown = acc.unknown, partial = acc.partial, unknownIds = acc.unknownIds }

@label "analyze: census bump unknown"
@description "Add `n` to the census accumulator's `unknown` count AND append the group's member ids to the Unknown worklist. Returns the updated census record."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaBumpUnknown : (acc: a) -> (n: b) -> (ids: c) -> a
anaBumpUnknown acc n ids =
  { total = acc.total, unknown = add acc.unknown n, partial = acc.partial, unknownIds = totConcat ids acc.unknownIds }

@label "analyze: census bump partial"
@description "Add `n` to the census accumulator's `partial` count, leaving the others. Returns the updated census record."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaBumpPartial : (acc: a) -> (n: b) -> a
anaBumpPartial acc n =
  { total = acc.total, unknown = acc.unknown, partial = add acc.partial n, unknownIds = acc.unknownIds }

@label "analyze: census one group"
@description "Fold one {ids, verdict} group result into the census accumulator: a Total group adds its member count to `total`; an Unknown group adds its count to `unknown` AND its ids to the Unknown worklist; a Partial group adds its count to `partial`. Counts by member-id count (the census counts functions, not SCCs)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaCensusOne : (r: a) -> (acc: b) -> b
anaCensusOne r acc =
  let n = length r.ids
  case r.verdict of
    Total -> anaBumpTotal acc n
    Unknown {} -> anaBumpUnknown acc n r.ids
    Partial {} -> anaBumpPartial acc n

@label "analyze: census fold"
@description "Fold anaCensusOne over every group result, threading the census accumulator."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaCensusGo : (results: a) -> (acc: b) -> b
anaCensusGo results acc =
  fold (\current r -> anaCensusOne r current) acc results

@label "analyze: count unanalyzable"
@description "Count the functions whose `analyzable` flag is False (the bodies that did not lower to core Expr — the 56 Err cases). Bucketed separately, NEVER folded into Total (D-3f-4)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaCountUnanalyzable : (functions: a) -> b
anaCountUnanalyzable functions =
  fold (\count f -> if f.analyzable then count else add count 1) 0 functions

@label "analyze: count unanalyzable (tail)"
@description "Recurse on the tail of the function list for anaCountUnanalyzable (keeps it free of case-in-let)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
@category "engine-internal"
anaCountUnanalyzableTail : (functions: a) -> b
anaCountUnanalyzableTail functions =
  case tail functions of
    Nothing -> 0
    Just rest -> anaCountUnanalyzable rest

@label "Totality census over a function registry"
@description "The ADVISORY totality census (the phase's headline output): run the analyze skeleton over a function list and aggregate into {total, unknown, partial, unanalyzable, unknownIds} — the per-bucket function COUNTS plus the Unknown id worklist (the triage list for the 3g flip: each Unknown is either a real fence — ≠0/ℕ guard, non-sub measure, outside-the-abstraction — or a checker gap to close before the global Unknown→reject flip). Counts are by member-id count (a 2-member Unknown group contributes 2). The Unanalyzable functions (bodies that did not lower to core Expr) are counted separately and NEVER folded into Total (D-3f-4). SOUND: the finite graph's reachability closure is exact; conservative call-graph over/under-approximations and unlowerable bodies still push toward Unknown/Unanalyzable, never a false Total — so the census is a sound LOWER bound on the work remaining before the flip. ADVISORY ONLY — does not touch the kernel, does not flip any verdict (D-3f-5)."
@tags "engine" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3f"
censusFunctions : (functions: a) -> b
censusFunctions functions =
  let results = analyzeFunctions functions
  let seed = { total = 0, unknown = 0, partial = 0, unknownIds = [] }
  let agg = anaCensusGo results seed
  let unanalyzable = anaCountUnanalyzable functions
  { total = agg.total, unknown = agg.unknown, partial = agg.partial, unanalyzable = unanalyzable, unknownIds = agg.unknownIds }


-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The KERNEL-GATE verdict projection (unified-static-analysis Phase 3g). The
-- proof-path gate consults ONE subject function's totality verdict as a string
-- TAG ("Total" | "Unknown" | "Partial"). `verdictTagFor` takes the subject +
-- its (pre-gathered, reachable) function records, follows the subject's
-- spelling-normalized forward reach, and returns Total only when every reached
-- body lowered and every SCC group among them is Total (TRANSITIVE since
-- 2026-10-02; before, only the subject's own group was read). A subject that did
-- not lower or was not gathered ⇒ "Unknown" — the soundness-conservative
-- default (NEVER a silent "Total"). The
-- TS seam (`subjectTotalityVerdict` in `kernel.ts`) does only the host-boundary
-- work a `.fenel` body cannot: resolve the registry's stored JSON-Logic bodies,
-- lower them to core `Expr`, and BFS-bound the reachable set (the census-runner
-- gather-host-data precedent). The DECISION — analyze + which group + which tag —
-- is 100% Fenel, here. 0 entity decls (string returns).
--
-- SCOPE (Phase 3g, 2026-06-21): this projection feeds the PROOF-PATH gate only —
-- it consults ONE subject function's verdict ON DEMAND (a bounded SCC), so it needs
-- NO whole-registry census. The UNCONDITIONAL GLOBAL flip (the type-checker
-- default-rejecting EVERY non-total function everywhere) STAYS DEFERRED: it would
-- false-reject the engine's OWN functions, whose interpreted census OVERFLOWS the
-- no-TCO host stack on the engine call graph (3f surprise #2 — `censusFunctions`
-- above hits the same wall). The global flip is gated on the COMPILED engine census
-- (a self-host / parser-substrate-adjacent track). See TODO.md `totality-checking`.
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@label "analyze: verdict tag of a Totality"
@description "Project a Totality verdict to its string tag: Total ⇒ \"Total\", Unknown ⇒ \"Unknown\", Partial ⇒ \"Partial\". The kernel-gate consumes the string (the `$`-key-free pre-computed fact the marshal seam threads into verifyProof). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3g"
@category "engine-internal"
anaVerdictToTag : (v: Totality) -> String
anaVerdictToTag v =
  case v of
    Total -> "Total"
    Unknown {} -> "Unknown"
    Partial {} -> "Partial"

@label "analyze: verdict tag of subject in results"
@description "Find the {ids, verdict} group result whose member-ids include `subjectId` and return its verdict TAG; a subject absent from every group ⇒ \"Unknown\" (the soundness-conservative default — never a silent Total). Walks the analyzeFunctions results. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3g"
@category "engine-internal"
anaVerdictTagOf : (subjectId: String) -> (results: a) -> String
anaVerdictTagOf subjectId results =
  let selected =
        fold
          (\state r ->
            if state.found then state
            else if elem subjectId r.ids
            then { found = True, tag = anaVerdictToTag r.verdict }
            else state)
          { found = False, tag = "Unknown" }
          results
  selected.tag

@label "analyze: reach step"
@description "Level-synchronous forward reachability over an adjacency list ({id, callees} rows): add the not-yet-visited callees of the frontier, then continue from them. Returns every node reachable in one or more steps (a node is in its own result iff it lies on a cycle). Callers pass fuel = node count + 1, which every productive level reduces by at least one new node, so the bound is never reached on a closed adjacency; if it were, the marker `$reach-fuel-exhausted` is returned with the partial set so the caller can refuse instead of under-approximating. Self-tail."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
anaReachStep : (adjacency: a) -> (frontier: b) -> (visited: b) -> (fuel: c) -> b
anaReachStep adjacency frontier visited fuel =
  let next = fold (\acc id -> fold (\current callee -> if elem callee visited then current else anaAddUnique callee current) acc (fold (\found row -> if eq row.id id then row.callees else found) [] adjacency)) [] frontier
  if eq (length next) 0 then visited
  else if eq fuel 0 then appendItem "$reach-fuel-exhausted" (concat visited next)
  else anaReachStep adjacency next (concat visited next) (sub fuel 1)

@label "analyze: SCC groups of reached records"
@description "Partition function records into strongly-connected groups from per-record forward reach sets ({id, reach} rows from anaReachStep): u and w share a group iff u == w, or each reaches the other. Each group is the checkMutualTotality input shape."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
anaReachedGroups : (records: a) -> (reaches: b) -> c
anaReachedGroups records reaches =
  let partitioned =
        fold
          (\state f ->
            if elem f.id state.assigned then state
            else
              let reachOfF = fold (\found row -> if eq row.id f.id then row.reach else found) [] reaches
              let members = filter (\g -> if eq g.id f.id then True else if elem g.id reachOfF then elem f.id (fold (\found row -> if eq row.id g.id then row.reach else found) [] reaches) else False) records
              { groups = appendItem members state.groups, assigned = totConcat (anaMapIds members) state.assigned })
          { groups = [], assigned = [] }
          records
  partitioned.groups

@label "Totality verdict tag for a subject function"
@description "THE KERNEL-GATE projection (unified-static-analysis Phase 3g): the totality verdict TAG (\"Total\" | \"Unknown\" | \"Partial\") for `subjectId`, run over the subject + its pre-gathered reachable function records (the {id, params, body, declaredPartial, analyzable} shape censusFunctions takes). TRANSITIVE (2026-10-02 — the earlier text claimed callee folding that analyzeFunctions never did, so a total caller of a non-terminating callee read Total): the call graph is built with spelling-normalized callees over EVERY gathered id (anaSpellingTargets — analyzable or not), the subject's forward reach is taken (anaReachStep), and the verdict is Total only when every reached record lowered (a reached Unanalyzable body ⇒ \"Unknown\") and every strongly-connected group among the reached records passes analyzeGroup (checkMutualTotality, or Partial for a declared @partial member). The subject's own group verdict is returned when it is not Total; a non-Total callee group makes a Total subject \"Unknown\" (callee groups are analyzed singletons first and only until the first non-Total one, since a multi-member size-change closure is the expensive step). A subject absent from the records, a reached id with no record, or an exhausted reach bound ⇒ \"Unknown\" — never a silent \"Total\". Ids outside the records stay sinks here: verdictTagForIn (the kernel entry) decides the bodyless natives the seam gathers before calling this, and passes only the bodied records. The TS seam threads the result into the kernel's SampleTestResult/PropForall arm, which REJECTS \"Unknown\"/\"Partial\" (vpSample). ADVISORY no longer — THIS is the consumer that makes the totality checker load-bearing."
@tags "engine" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3g"
verdictTagFor : (subjectId: String) -> (functions: a) -> String
verdictTagFor subjectId functions =
  let knownIds = anaMapIds functions
  let adjacency = map (\f -> { id = f.id, callees = if f.analyzable then analyzeCallees f.body knownIds else [] }) functions
  anaVerdictTagOver subjectId functions adjacency

@label "analyze: verdict tag over an adjacency"
@description "verdictTagFor's decision over a precomputed adjacency ({id, callees} rows whose callees are ids of `functions`): the subject's forward reach, the refusal of a missing or unlowered reached record, and the SCC verdicts (own group first, then the callee groups, singletons before multi-member groups). verdictTagForIn calls it with callees resolved once against the whole registry and restricted to the bodied records."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
anaVerdictTagOver : (subjectId: String) -> (functions: a) -> (adjacency: b) -> String
anaVerdictTagOver subjectId functions adjacency =
  let fuel = add (length functions) 1
  let reached = anaAddUnique subjectId (anaReachStep adjacency (appendItem subjectId []) [] fuel)
  let records = filter (\f -> elem f.id reached) functions
  if not (eq (length records) (length reached)) then "Unknown"
  else if gt (length (filter (\f -> not f.analyzable) records)) 0 then "Unknown"
  else
    let reaches = map (\f -> { id = f.id, reach = anaReachStep adjacency (appendItem f.id []) [] fuel }) records
    let groups = anaReachedGroups records reaches
    let own = anaVerdictTagOf subjectId (anaAnalyzeGroups (filter (\g -> elem subjectId (anaMapIds g)) groups))
    if not (eq own "Total") then own
    else
      fold
        (\tag g ->
          if not (eq tag "Total") then tag
          else if elem subjectId (anaMapIds g) then tag
          else if eq (anaVerdictTagOf (fromMaybe "" (head (anaMapIds g))) (anaAnalyzeGroups (appendItem g []))) "Total" then "Total"
          else "Unknown")
        "Total"
        (concat (filter (\g -> eq (length g) 1) groups) (filter (\g -> gt (length g) 1) groups))

@label "analyze: applied callee of an apply form"
@description "The applied reference of one `$ callee args…` form for anaAppliedRefsIn: when the callee is a variable whose root (totSpellingRoot) no binder in `bound` binds, append {spelling, argc} with argc the number of arguments applied to it. A bound callee (a parameter, a pattern variable, a local closure), a lambda literal and a computed callee are left to the group audit (totUncheckedApply)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
anaAppliedCallee : (bound: a) -> (acc: b) -> (args: c) -> b
anaAppliedCallee bound acc args =
  case head args of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just callee ->
      case callee of
        EVar { name = n } -> if elem (totSpellingRoot n) bound then acc else appendItem { spelling = n, argc = sub (length args) 1 } acc
        _ -> acc

@label "analyze: applied reference of a call node"
@description "The applied reference a call node `f args` contributes for anaAppliedRefsIn: none for the `if` guard form or a list literal's synthetic appendItem (totIsListLiteral, a construction); the callee of the `$` apply form (anaAppliedCallee); a `$dyn:` var-head call when no binder in `bound` binds its root; every other string head. Each is the record {spelling, argc}."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
anaAppliedHead : (bound: a) -> (acc: b) -> (e: (Expr Any)) -> (f: String) -> (args: c) -> b
anaAppliedHead bound acc e f args =
  if and (eq f "if") (not (eq (lookup e "structural") (Just false))) then acc
  else if totIsListLiteral e then acc
  else if eq f "$" then anaAppliedCallee bound acc args
  else if startsWith f "$dyn:" then (if elem (totSpellingRoot f) bound then acc else appendItem { spelling = f, argc = length args } acc)
  else appendItem { spelling = f, argc = length args } acc

@label "analyze: applied references in a body"
@description "Collect, as {spelling, argc} records, every reference the core Expr applies to arguments without a binder in `bound` providing it (anaAppliedHead): each string call head (except the `if` form and a list literal's synthetic appendItem), the variable callee of a `$` apply, and each `$dyn:` var-head call, with the number of arguments applied. The kernel-gate entry starts `bound` at the function's params; lambda params and arm pattern vars extend it, so a bound callee is left to the group audit (totUncheckedReference: a callback is refused, a checked local closure accepted). Arm guards are walked like bodies."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
anaAppliedRefsIn : (bound: a) -> (acc: b) -> (e: (Expr Any)) -> b
anaAppliedRefsIn bound acc e =
  case e of
    ELit { value = _ } -> acc
    EVar { name = _ } -> acc
    ECall { fnId = f, args = args } -> fold (\current a -> anaAppliedRefsIn bound current a) (anaAppliedHead bound acc e f args) args
    ELambda { params = ps, body = bd } -> anaAppliedRefsIn (totAppendAll ps bound) acc bd
    EMatch { scrutinee = s, arms = arms } -> fold (\current arm -> anaAppliedRefsInArm (totCollectAllVars arm.pattern bound) current arm) (anaAppliedRefsIn bound acc s) arms
    EConstruct { args = args } -> fold (\current a -> anaAppliedRefsIn bound current a) acc args
    ERecord { fields = fields } -> fold (\current f -> anaAppliedRefsIn bound current f.value) acc fields

@label "analyze: applied references in a match arm"
@description "anaAppliedRefsIn over one match arm, `bound` already extended by the arm's pattern variables: its guard when present (it runs before the body), then its body."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
anaAppliedRefsInArm : (bound: a) -> (acc: b) -> (arm: c) -> b
anaAppliedRefsInArm bound acc arm =
  case lookup arm "guard" of
    Nothing -> anaAppliedRefsIn bound acc arm.body
    Just guard -> anaAppliedRefsIn bound (anaAppliedRefsIn bound acc guard) arm.body

@label "analyze: applied reference over-applies a bodied function"
@description "True when one of `targets` is a bodied function whose param count (`arities`, a record from id to param count built over the gathered bodied records) is below `argc`. The evaluator binds a bodied callee's params, evaluates its body and applies any leftover arguments to the result when it is callable (json-logic.ts, the eta-reduction spill): an invocation of a value the analysis never checked. A native receives every argument and never spills, so natives are absent from `arities`."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
anaOverApplies : (targets: a) -> (argc: Number) -> (arities: b) -> Bool
anaOverApplies targets argc arities =
  fold (\found t -> if found then True else anaOverAppliesOne t argc arities) False targets

@label "analyze: applied reference over-applies one function"
@description "True when `t` has a param count in `arities` (it is a gathered bodied function) below `argc` (anaOverApplies)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
anaOverAppliesOne : (t: String) -> (argc: Number) -> (arities: a) -> Bool
anaOverAppliesOne t argc arities =
  case mapGet arities t of
    Nothing -> False
    Just n -> gt argc n

@label "analyze: body applies an unchecked reference"
@description "True when an applied reference of the record's body (anaAppliedRefsIn, `bound` starting at its params) denotes no registry id (anaSpellingTargets against `registryIds`; `joined` is anaJoinedIds registryIds) — a class-method name resolved by dispatch, a host leaf the registry does not hold, a bundle or instance member path (`m.k.run`), or a free local recursive binding, any of which may run code the analysis never gathered — or over-applies a bodied function (anaOverApplies: the extra arguments invoke its result)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
anaAppliesUnchecked : (f: a) -> (registryIds: b) -> (joined: String) -> (arities: c) -> Bool
anaAppliesUnchecked f registryIds joined arities =
  fold (\found r -> if found then True else anaRefUnchecked r registryIds joined arities) False (anaAppliedRefsIn f.params [] f.body)

@label "analyze: applied reference is unchecked"
@description "True when the applied reference `r` ({spelling, argc}) denotes no registry id, or over-applies a gathered bodied function (anaOverApplies)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis"
@category "engine-internal"
anaRefUnchecked : (r: a) -> (registryIds: b) -> (joined: String) -> (arities: c) -> Bool
anaRefUnchecked r registryIds joined arities =
  let targets = anaSpellingTargets r.spelling registryIds joined
  if eq (length targets) 0 then True else anaOverApplies targets r.argc arities

-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- NATIVE LEAVES (2026-10-03). A registered function with no body (a native
-- or host leaf) is a termination SINK only when it is a CERTIFIED terminating
-- leaf. The kernel seam gathers each reached bodyless function as a record
-- marked `native = True` (it never decides anything about it); the list below is
-- the certification, as Fenel data. A native that evaluates caller-supplied code
-- or calls back into the evaluator is NOT certified (evaluator re-entry: running
-- a closure, a function id, an expression value, or the predicates a type or a
-- set carries), nor is one that may wait forever; nor is any native this list
-- does not name (fail-closed: a new native is Unknown until certified here).
-- Audit (2026-10-03, every bodyless system-registry function): uncertified are
-- std:evalExpr / std:validateValue / std:parseInput (evaluate an expression or a
-- type's refinements), all of control:* (run a function id; while_true / repeat
-- loop), io:read (waits for input) and io:call_function, the sampling and
-- rendering natives that invoke the closure a Sound / Animation / Movie /
-- Behavior / Game / Track carries (sound:sampleSound/renderSound,
-- animation:sampleAnim/renderAnim, movie:sampleMovie/renderMovie,
-- events:_accumFold/sampleBehavior, games:gameStateAt/_gameViewAt,
-- track:sampleTrackAt), every set:* native except the All/None/Enum/Interval/
-- Pattern membership leaves (the rest reach `$where` predicate evaluation or a
-- named type's refinements), all of prover:* and evaluator-strategies:*,
-- kernel:verify, and migration:roundtripCheck/forwardTotalCheck (apply a
-- migration's functions). Certified natives that delegate to engine Fenel bodies
-- on DATA (compile-*:* run the compiler passes over a program without running
-- it; storage containment filters call storage:jsonContains) trust those bodies
-- to terminate.
-- Second audit (2026-10-03, loop bounds and host re-entry). A native whose loop
-- bound is a caller-supplied number with no enforced safe-integer bound can run
-- forever on finite input: a JS number counter stalls at 2^53 (y + 1 === y). The
-- image routines of image-ops.ts loop `y < height` / `x < width` over the
-- caller's image record, and `new Array(width * height)` bounds nothing when
-- width is 0 (or tiny) and height huge, so 35 of them are uncertified:
-- Grayscale, Invert, Brightness, Contrast, Saturate, HueRotate, Sepia, Threshold,
-- Posterize, Gamma, Opacity, Red/Green/BlueChannel, SwapRedBlue, SwapRedGreen,
-- Vignette (mapPixels); BoxBlur, GaussianBlur, Sharpen, Emboss (convolve);
-- EdgeDetect, Median, Dither, Crop (fractional width), FlipHorizontal,
-- FlipVertical, Rotate90, Rotate270, Transpose, Pixelate, Overlay, Multiply,
-- Screen, Difference. Kept: imageResize, imageSolid, imageGradient,
-- imageCheckerboard (integer dimensions >= 1 whose product new Array accepts,
-- so each loop is below 2^32), imageRotate180 and imageNoise (loop i < w*h
-- after that allocation), imageSample (no loop). Every other certified native
-- loops only over its argument data (a list, a string, a record's keys) or
-- calls a host builtin whose work is bounded by its result (String repeat and
-- padStart throw RangeError past the maximum string length; "".repeat(n) and
-- slice return at once). Also uncertified: io:emit (its handler runs
-- events:emitEvent, whose trigger dispatch runs the event's subscribers) and
-- telegram:startCollectorEntry (its handler runs telegram:startTelegramForm with
-- the caller's hook functions) — both re-enter the evaluator — and
-- templates:render_template (declared to evaluate the template function its
-- caller names by slug; it has no implementation today, so a call throws). Trusted, not
-- re-checked: an IO leaf's single host act returns (a timeout, a wake time or a
-- RangeError bounds it); io:sleep suspends the run until a wake time the Date
-- range bounds.
-- recipe-functions S1 (2026-10-18): std:includes, std:unique and
-- std:distinctCount became Fenel-bodied (membership on structural `eq`), so
-- they left this list and the analysis walks their bodies; std:elem stays a
-- certified bodyless native (its array arm now compares with structuralEq,
-- which recurses only over its argument data).
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@label "analyze: certified terminating native leaves"
@description "The ids of the bodyless registry functions certified as terminating leaves (the native-leaves block above): a native that only computes on its argument data or performs one host IO act, never evaluating caller-supplied code. A reached bodyless function whose id is not listed makes the kernel-gate verdict Unknown (verdictTagForIn). Takes a unit argument so a body reads the list, not a reference to it."
@tags "engine" "analyze" "unified-static-analysis"
anaCertifiedNativeLeaves : (unit: a) -> List String
anaCertifiedNativeLeaves unit =
